  "goodToKnow": "Der Unmut is displeasure or discontent: auf Unmut stoßen (to meet with displeasure), seinem Unmut Luft machen (to vent one's displeasure), wachsender Unmut. It's a favourite of news reports about unpopular decisions. Der Mut now means courage, but originally meant mood or mind, preserved in Unmut, Übermut (high spirits), Wehmut (melancholy) and Gemüt. It has no plural."
